  },
  "open-questions": {
   "x": 1520,
   "y": 0,
   "text": "Open questions for the product owner\n\nNone. Every question was answered in Revision 1.",
   "w": 560,
   "fill": "teal",
   "size": 24
  },
  "revision-1": {
   "x": 1520,
   "y": 1400,
   "w": 560,
   "fill": "blue",
   "text": "Revision 1 · 19 Nov 2026\n\n1. Manager shows its seeded 15 permissions everywhere. The matrix editor (light and dark) has 3 pending changes: user.delete and role.update added, content.delete_article removed.\n2. Password expiry stays at 90 days. “needs API” tags on the expiring card and on the users list Status column. Security adds “Passwords expire every 90 days.”\n3. Account expiry: no screen showed it, so nothing was removed. Only password expiry appears.\n4. User forms list only roles the viewer can grant, with a helper line. The superuser switch is tagged “visible to superusers only”. New: create form as a manager.\n5. New: Sign out everywhere confirmation (“You’ll be signed out on this device too.”) and Sign in with “You’ve been signed out everywhere.”\n6. Role distribution footnote added.\n7. Recent sign-ins shows the last 10, newest first, with relative times and the full date on hover.\n8. Trees show a child group: Support under Operational, Articles under Content.\n9. New: unverified user detail with “Resend verification email” and its toast.\n10. Removed “Unauthorized – signed out”.\n11. Avatars stay initials only. There were no upload controls to remove."
  },
  "how-to": {
   "x": 1520,
   "y": 900,
   "text": "Engineer tags\n\nDashed amber tags are notes for engineers, not UI. “needs API” marks data that needs a backend endpoint that doesn’t exist yet. “visible to superusers only” marks a control only superusers see.\n\nArtboards are named NN · Group · Screen · Size · Theme.",
   "w": 560,
   "fill": "gray",
   "size": "s"
  },
